From: AutoWorkflows contributors
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-fullconenat-sonic: add per-device NAT1 access control

Add an optional device list that restricts fullcone NAT (NAT1) mapping
creation to explicitly listed devices. Unlisted devices of a zone keep
ordinary masquerading, so they are not reachable from the internet through
this mapping. The list is empty by default while the switch is off, which
preserves the previous behaviour.

Devices are chosen by MAC address from the hosts known to dnsmasq (DHCP
leases, static leases and the neighbour table) and are resolved to the
current IP address of the device whenever the page is saved, because the
firewall consumes addresses. Fixed addresses may be entered as plain IP
addresses or subnets instead and are used as-is. Every entry shows whether
the device has a static lease and whether it currently has a usable
address; a per-entry button refreshes the resolved addresses on demand.

The page is a standalone view so that it does not depend on the layout of
the firewall zone page, and it reuses the existing translation catalogue of
this package for its added strings.

Reading the dhcp configuration for the static lease hints requires read
access, which the new ACL description grants.

